Source: organizer
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Raajeshwar Elagovan <raajeshwar43@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-python, python3
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/RaajeshwarElagovan/organizer
Rules-Requires-Root: no
X-Python3-Version: >= 3.8

Package: organizer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: systemd, file
Description: report-only file classifier with a self-learning memory
 organizer scans a directory and proposes a folder structure and a per-file
 action (move, archive, delete, keep, review) from names, types and stat()
 metadata only. It never reads file contents and never moves, renames or
 deletes user files: applying a report is left to the user or an external
 agent reading the JSON. On kernels with Landlock the daemon and CLI restrict
 their own writes to ~/.config/organizer, ~/.local/share/organizer and the
 socket directory.
 .
 A systemd --user unit is shipped in /usr/lib/systemd/user; it is not enabled
 automatically (run `systemctl --user enable --now organizer`). Without the
 daemon the CLI runs in-process.
 .
 The optional AI stage uses the external `claude` CLI (Claude Code), which is
 not part of this package; without it the rule engine still works and
 undecided entries are reported as `review`.
